CORE
main.c
--unwind 2 --rounds 4 --por --allow-pointer-unsoundness
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
Narrowing is sound only because nothing observes the bits it drops, so the
analysis bails on any use of a shared object outside a byte_extract or
byte_update. Here the mutex is copied whole into `snapshot`, which is exactly
such a use.

The bail is observable: this program produces 24071 variables and 83845 clauses
both with narrowing on and with --no-narrow-shared, i.e. the narrowed path
leaves it completely alone, whereas narrow_shared_mutex -- the same program
without the copy -- drops from 63131 clauses to 26427.
